      "date": "2000-09",
      "kind": "conversion",
      "description": "In September 2000 the interior of the 82-year-old Coliseum Theater was being demolished and its asbestos removed, as Village Properties converted it to housing and shops with a full seismic upgrade and the front kept. The theater had been badly damaged in the October 17, 1989 earthquake and empty for more than ten years.",
      "source": "sf-neighborhood-newspapers-richmondreview1212rich-n2"
